  "method_recommendations": {
    "recommendations": [
      "energy_kwh is NOT normally distributed (heavy-tailed, right-skewed). Use median/IQR rather than mean/std for robust baselines.",
      "lnenergy (log-kWh) is approximately log-normally distributed. Regression and Z-scores on log scale are appropriate.",
      "Strong time-of-day effect (peak/trough ratio=2.35x). Baseline model must condition on hour-of-day.",
      "Significant day-of-week effect (Kruskal-Wallis p<0.05). Baseline must include day-of-week.",
      "Temporal gaps (missing hours) are present in all households. Rolling features must use a minimum-observations guard to avoid misleading baselines over gaps.",
      "Recommended anomaly signals: (1) per-household Z-score on lnenergy, (2) IQR fence on energy_kwh, (3) residual from rolling-window or regression-predicted baseline."
    ]
  }
